# api-surface.tflw — `T-1b` (tflw `D1372`): the one `crawl` in the discovered tree. The documented
# API and every request this run's own tests made, re-issued under each other declared principal,
# with the authorization family judging every response. `tflw-acceptance/security/crawl.tflw` is the
# graded corpus (planted leaks, `VULN_MODE=1`); this is the journey — the clean app, walked as a
# customer, and nothing leaking is the answer.
#
# **Why not the storefront's spider, which the plan named.** Measured before writing it: the
# storefront is client-rendered, so a fetching spider reads one shell and no link (tflw declares
# that blind spot itself, and `tests/.tflw-ui/scan.tflw` records the same for the page); and the
# only families a crawl may assert are security, authorization and input handling. On that shell
# the security family either has no applicable rule at the critical floor (no cookie, no CORS
# header — `D285` fails that) or fires `csp-missing`, which the security corpus's spider test uses
# as its positive control. Authorization is the family with something to say about every route.
#
# **`expect`, and the first run is why it can be.** It reached 14 routes of the clean app and failed
# six as having *no power to fail*: `/health`, a profile avatar, an empty list — bodies with no root
# `id` give the authorization rules nothing to read. A crawl reaches routes a document chose, so some
# always have that shape, and `D285` judged per response made a hard assertion over any real API
# unwritable. tflw's `M247-02` (gap `G4`) asks `D285` of the surface instead: such a route reports
# *not applicable on this route*, and the assertion fails only if it applied on none.
#
# `/vuln/**` is excluded: under `VULN_MODE=1` it holds the corpus's planted leaks, which are
# `crawl.tflw`'s to grade, not this file's. `probe mutating` is not granted in `env local`, so every
# synthesized write is enumerated, disclosed and not sent. Tagged `@scan`, which no smoke tier names.

@scan @authz
crawl "the documented API and this run's traffic, walked as a customer" as peer
  seed openapi root "/openapi.json"
  seed traffic
  exclude "/v1/vuln/**"
  exclude "/v1/contract-demo/*"
  expect response has no critical authorization violations
